# A customer's security questionnaire, answered from our own documents and
# checked against our infrastructure: Tamsin Labs answering twelve questions
# from Harrowgate Regional Health, as of 2026-10-01.
#
# B-E and H-J are agent cells: the answer, an explanation the customer can
# read, the passage it rests on, which configuration claim it makes, whether
# a person must decide something before it goes out, a second agent's review,
# and the date of time-bound evidence such as a pen test. F tests the claim
# the agent named against the Terraform and exports in infra/
# (checks/config.py) and re-runs when infra/ changes; G marks any answer the
# check contradicts, a Yes beside a failing configuration. A passing check
# doesn't make the whole answer true: daily backups pass, but nothing shows
# a restore test. The named cells count the answers and say whether the
# questionnaire is ready to send.
#
# Select B2:J13 and Run Selection to fill the agent cells. The company,
# documents and infrastructure are synthetic.
instructions = You are on Tamsin Labs's security team answering a customer's security questionnaire as of 2026-10-01. Answer only from policies/, reports/ and the Terraform and exports in infra/. Use the current version of each policy: a newer version supersedes an older one from its effective date. Answer Yes only if our documents say so and, where the answer is a configuration claim, the configuration in infra/ agrees; if they disagree, answer Partial and name what falls short. A time-bound activity (a test, an audit, a review) counts only if its evidence falls within the period the question asks about. Never commit to more than our documents do. If our documents don't answer the question, answer Not found. Answer in exactly the form the question asks for, with no preamble; cite the passage your answer rests on with cite_cell.
A1 = Question
B1 = Answer: Yes, No, Partial or N/A
C1 = Explanation for the customer, in one or two sentences
D1 = The passage the answer rests on, verbatim
E1 = Configuration claim the answer makes: one of None, Encryption at rest, MFA, Branch protection, Backups
F1 = Configuration check
G1 = Answer and check
H1 = Does a person need to decide something before this goes out (anything Not found, evidence out of date, or a commitment beyond our documents)? Yes or No
I1 = Review the answer another agent gave against our documents, and say agree or disagree
J1 = Evidence date, for an answer resting on a time-bound activity such as a test or an audit, as YYYY-MM-DD; Not found otherwise
A2 = HRH-01: Is customer data encrypted at rest in every production data store?
B2 = @claude('{instructions} Question: {$A2}. {B$1}')
C2 = @claude('{instructions} Question: {$A2}. {C$1}')
D2 = @claude('{instructions} Question: {$A2}. {D$1}')
E2 = @claude('{instructions} Question: {$A2}. {E$1}')
H2 = @claude('{instructions} Question: {$A2}. {H$1}')
J2 = @claude('{instructions} Question: {$A2}. {J$1}')
I2 = @claude('{instructions} Question: {$A2}. Another agent answered {B2}: {C2} {I$1}')
F2 = $ python3 checks/config.py {E2} # watch: infra/**
G2 = = if({F2} == 'n/a', 'n/a', if(and({B2} == 'Yes', {F2} != 'pass'), 'CONTRADICTED', 'ok'))
